===== Flashing =====

{{:meta:48px-dialog-warning.svg.png |}} Flashing OpenWrt void your warranty.\\
Use your own risk!

Currently you can only install OpenWrt by using stock webshell or U-Boot  \\
Sysupgrade is supported by device and is the recommended way of upgrading.

M1200AC only can use U-Boot method.


==== OEM installation using the stock web shell ====

{{:meta:48px-dialog-warning.svg.png |}} If device is bricked,\\
The only way to debrick is via UART


Before you start, setup tftp server, prepare sysupgrade.bin for WF2881 and rename it to fw.bin
 
  - upgrade router to version 1.8.0 (since 1.8.1 secret password seems to be changed, just downgrade to 1.8.0)
  - login router admin page (default address http://192.168.1.1)
  - go to stock web shell /syscmd.htm 
  - type secret password 'netis-yun' in input box 
  - type 'cd /tmp && tftp -g -r fw.bin <your tftp server ip>'
  - check your firmware downloaded completely with 'ls -all /tmp/fw.bin' (file size check)
  - 'mtd_write write /tmp/fw.bin mtd4 && reboot'


==== OEM installation using the TFTP method ====

The device can be flashed via bootloader (U-Boot), serial connection is needed.\\
Settings: 57600, 8N1

  - Select option 2
  - If you see warning, Press 'Y' 
  - Set your desired tftp client ip, server ip, file name (openwrt-ramips-mt7621-WF-2881-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin)

